mode: "100644"
text: "# Hooks, retention, captions + two worked Shorts\n\n## Frame-one hook patterns (must read silently)\nPut the words on screen frame one; assume no sound.\n- **Open loop:** \"The invoicing mistake that cost me €4,000.\"\n- **Contrarian:** \"Posting daily is killing your Shorts.\"\n- **Problem call-out:** \"If your Shorts die at 200 views, it's this.\"\n- **POV:** \"POV: it's the 28th and three clients haven't paid.\"\n- **Number:** \"3 freelance-tax rules. The last one is free money.\"\nMatch the hook's promise to the payoff — bait-and-switch tanks retention and satisfaction.\n\n## Retention tactics (Rung 2)\n- Cut the first half-second of any dull opening; it often lifts retention noticeably.\n- New visual or info beat every 1–2 seconds; kill establishing shots.\n- Keep CTAs tiny — a 3-second CTA is ~10% of a 30s Short. Prefer a loop over a long sign-off.\n- Build a **conceptual loop** so the end feeds the start (chase >100% avg % viewed).\n\n## Length selection\nDesign the idea, then pick the shortest complete length. Default 15–35s for most niches; go to\n50–90s only if retention data proves viewers stay. Up to 3 min is allowed but rarely optimal.\n\n## Caption spec\nMost viewers are on mute. Burn in captions: ~2 lines per frame, 32–42 chars per line, away from\nthe screen edges (and the Shorts UI). Captions also get indexed for Shorts search.\n\n## Worked example 1 — blunt indie-founder voice (~18s)\n```\n0:00  ON-SCREEN: \"I almost missed €4,000 in tax.\"\n0:00  VO: \"Almost missed four grand in tax this year. Not proud of it.\"\n0:03  SHOT: fast screen-record of a messy spreadsheet\n0:04  VO: \"Tracked income. Didn't track the set-aside.\"\n0:08  ON-SCREEN: \"30% of every invoice -> separate account, same day.\"\n0:09  VO: \"Thirty percent, separate account, the day it lands.\"\n0:13  VO: \"Boring. Works. Saved my April.\"\n0:15  LOOP line: \"Almost missed four grand...\" (cuts to frame one)\nTITLE: \"The 30% rule that saves freelancers at tax time\" (keyword-rich for Shorts search)\nCAPTIONS: burned in, 2 lines max. ANGLE: the same-day rule, not generic \"save for tax.\"\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — warm studio voice (~30s)\n```\n0:00  ON-SCREEN: \"How we stopped dreading tax season\"\n0:00  VO: \"If tax season makes your stomach drop -- this helps.\"\n0:04  SHOT: calm desk, hands, a banking app\n0:05  VO: \"We changed one thing. The panic went away.\"\n0:10  ON-SCREEN: \"A second account, labelled Tax.\"\n0:11  VO: \"Open a second account. Call it Tax.\"\n0:17  ON-SCREEN: \"Auto-move 30% the day an invoice clears.\"\n0:18  VO: \"Move thirty percent the moment a client pays. You never see it, never spend it.\"\n0:26  LOOP line: \"If tax season makes your stomach drop...\" (back to frame one)\nTITLE: \"The calm way to handle freelance tax (2 steps)\"\nCAPTIONS: burned in. BRIDGE: pin the long-form 'full freelance finance setup' on the channel.\n```\n\nBoth: read brand-profile + voice-builder first; shootable (on-screen text, VO, shots); one idea;\nintentional loop; keyword-rich title; human films/edits. Sibling short-form writers for cross-\nposting the same idea: reels-script, tiktok-script (adapt natively, don't reuse watermarked files).\n"
